{% include 'header.liquid' %}

<section id="landing">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="landing-content">
      <h1>
        The 3D digital twin for <span class="text-pink">campus-wide</span> energy systems
      </h1>
      <p>
        One network, one view. Connect live data to intuitive visualisations, analyses and what-if simulations. 
      </p>
      <div class="landing-buttons">
        <a href="https://bronscode.nl/contact" class="btn">Request demo</a>
        <a href="#features" class="btn btn-outline">See how it works</a>
      </div>
      <img class="landing-images-front" src="/img/microgrid_sc.png">
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="problem">
  <div class="container">

    <div class="section-heading">
      <div>
        <span class="section-descriptor">Problem</span>
        <h2>Energy systems are becoming more complex.</h2>
      </div>
      <p>Campus energy managers face growing grid congestion, increasingly complex energy systems, changing regulations and ambitious sustainability goals. At the same time, information is often distributed across different systems, organisations and stakeholders.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="problem-grid">
      <div class="problem-item">
        <span class="problem-number">01</span>
        <h3>Grid congestion</h3>
        <p>Expanding or upgrading connections is becoming increasingly difficult, forcing campuses to make better use of existing infrastructure.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="problem-item">
        <span class="problem-number">02</span>
        <h3>System complexity</h3>
        <p>More energy assets, energy carriers and sustainability goals make campus energy systems harder to understand and manage.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="problem-item">
        <span class="problem-number">03</span>
        <h3>Fragmented information</h3>
        <p>Relevant information is distributed across systems, organisations and stakeholders, making it difficult to build a shared picture.</p>
      </div>

    </div>

    <div class="problem-highlight">
      <span>WHAT'S NEEDED?</span>
      <p>A shared, decision-ready view of the energy system with the ability to explore the impact of changes before they are implemented.
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<section id="features">
  <div class="container">
  <span class="section-descriptor">Solution</span>

    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2>How does it work?</h2>
      <p>MICROGRID brings the energy system together in three steps.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="features-list">

      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-number">01</div>
        <div class="feature-content">
          <h3>Connect</h3>
          <p>
            Bring spatial, operational and network data together.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-icon">
          {% include "img/icons-connect.svg" %}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-number">02</div>
        <div class="feature-content">
          <h3>Understand</h3>
          <p>
            Explore infrastructure, topology and energy flows in an interactive 3D environment.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-icon">
          {% include "img/icons-cube.svg" %}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="feature">
        <div class="feature-number">03</div>
        <div class="feature-content">
          <h3>Explore</h3>
          <p>
            Visualise proposed changes and investigate their potential impact.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-icon">
          {% include "img/icons-chart.svg" %}
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="why-it-works">
  <div class="container">
    <span class="section-descriptor">Benefits</span>
    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2>Why does it work?</h2>
      <p>
        MICROGRID turns fragmented information into a shared environment for understanding and exploring energy systems.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="why-grid">

      <div class="why-image">
        <img src="/img/microgrid_sc_focus.png" alt="Visual 3D representation of the energy system, with one building highlighted">
      </div>

      <div class="why-principles">

        <div class="why-item">
          <span class="why-number">01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>One shared view</h3>
            <p>
              Bring fragmented information into one spatial and operational context.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="why-item">
          <span class="why-number">02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Understand before you change</h3>
            <p>
              Explore the existing system and its relationships before making changes.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="why-item">
          <span class="why-number">03</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Explore together</h3>
            <p>
              Give different stakeholders a common environment for discussing proposed changes and their potential consequences.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section id="cases">
  <div class="container">

    <div class="section-heading">
      <h2>Where is it used?</h2>
      <p>
        MICROGRID is currently being developed and applied at Arnhems Buiten, an electricity campus in Arnhem.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="cases-grid">

      <article class="case-card">
        <a href="/en/arnhems-buiten/" class="case-image">
          <img src="/img/dnv_building.png" alt="Arnhems Buiten electricity campus">
        </a>

        <div class="case-content">
          <div class="section-descriptor">ARNHEMS BUITEN</div>
          <h3>Digital twin for a complex electricity campus.</h3>
          <p>
            MICROGRID was first developed at Arnhems Buiten Electricity Campus. The project was awarded through the competitive European open call for the Hedge-IoT ecosystem, recognising both the need for better tools in campus energy management and the strength of MICROGRID as a practical, scalable solution.
          </p>
          <a href="/en/arnhems-buiten/" class="case-link">
            Explore the case
            <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </article>

    </div>

  </div>
</section>

